From e2ff7d73bcd174fa03155f04b1f4564cb7cd1267 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Allen <callen.23dc@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:05:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] screencast: cancel a capture before its buffer goes back
 to PipeWire

When the stream stops streaming, or PipeWire removes the buffer being
captured into, the capture into it carried on: a delayed capture's
timer stayed armed, and an ext frame in flight stayed alive. Its
listener then acted on whatever the cast was capturing by the time the
frame finished. After a pause and resume, STREAMING dequeues a new
buffer and creates a second frame on the session, a protocol error
(duplicate_frame) under a compositor that checks; under one that
doesn't, the old frame's ready destroys the new frame and queues the
new buffer, never captured, as a complete frame. The delayed capture
of the new buffer then finds no buffer ("ext: started frame without
buffer"), and the stream may stall.

Keep the delayed capture's timer, and cancel the capture, the timer
and the frame, whenever the stream leaves STREAMING and before the
current buffer is removed. The events of a destroyed frame are never
dispatched, so a frame's events always belong to the current capture.
Record a wlr-screencopy frame when it is created rather than at its
first event, so that it can be cancelled too.
---
 include/screencast_common.h          |  1 +
 include/wlr_screencast.h             |  1 +
 src/screencast/pipewire_screencast.c | 20 +++++++++++---------
 src/screencast/screencast.c          |  3 ++-
 src/screencast/wlr_screencast.c      | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 src/screencast/wlr_screencopy.c      |  1 +
 6 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

